{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Siobhan Bayan. We met in the hospital back in February. Can you confirm your full name and date of birth for me?",
   "start": 0.05,
   "end": 8.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Call it Mansur, September 8, 1967.",
   "start": 9.07,
   "end": 12.09
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks, Mr. Mansur. The front desk mentioned you had a new insurance card. Yeah, how we switched plans.",
   "start": 13.46,
   "end": 19.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "The member ID is K, as in kilo -7 -3 -0 -9 -2 -5 -8.",
   "start": 19.82,
   "end": 24.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Got it. I'll make sure they update it. So it's been about 8 months since your stent on February 11th. How are you doing overall?",
   "start": 24.74,
   "end": 31.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Heart -wise, good. No chest pain at all since the stent. I finished cardiac rehab in June, and I'm walking 30 minutes most days.",
   "start": 32.62,
   "end": 39.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's excellent. Any shortness of breath with the walking?",
   "start": 40.71,
   "end": 43.45
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, I'm fine. The kids at Roosevelt High School keep me moving too. I teach chemistry there.",
   "start": 44.27,
   "end": 49.73
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Huh? That'll do it. Your portal message said you had a problem with the atorvastatin.",
   "start": 50.63,
   "end": 55.11
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, so my thighs and calves were aching, both legs, like I'd run a marathon. It started maybe two months after the hospital. I put up with it, but about three weeks ago I just stopped taking it. I'm sorry, I know I should have called first.",
   "start": 55.88,
   "end": 68.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "No need to apologize, I'm glad you're telling me. What dose were you taking?",
   "start": 69.2,
   "end": 73.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "40 milligrams. No, wait, it's the big one. 80 milligrams.",
   "start": 73.86,
   "end": 77.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Right, 80 is what we started in the hospital. And since you stopped it, how are the legs?",
   "start": 78.48,
   "end": 83.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "much better maybe 90 % gone any",
   "start": 83.18,
   "end": 87.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "muscle weakness trouble getting up from a chair or dark cola -colored urine",
   "start": 87.16,
   "end": 91.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "know nothing like that good and",
   "start": 91.4,
   "end": 95.05
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "the other medicines the aspirin clopidogrel and metoprolol you're still taking",
   "start": 95.05,
   "end": 99.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "those aspirin 81 once a day clopidogrel 75 once a day and the metoprolol 25 milligrams once a day I haven't missed any of those great",
   "start": 99.43,
   "end": 110.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "any bleeding or bruising on the two blood thinners.",
   "start": 110.27,
   "end": 113.07
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Some small bruises on my arms, nothing serious.",
   "start": 113.49,
   "end": 116.31
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's common on those two, and you're still allergic to sulfa drugs.",
   "start": 117.34,
   "end": 120.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, I get a rash all over.",
   "start": 121.52,
   "end": 123.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, your blood pressure today is 124 over 76, pulse 62. Heart has a regular rhythm, no murmur. Lungs are clear. The spot on your right wrist where we put the catheter in is well -heeled. No tenderness in your thigh or calf muscles, goals, and your leg strength is normal. Good. Your labs from last week, so after about two weeks off the statin, show an LDL of 118. For someone with a stent, we want the LDL under 55, so that's well above goal. Your CK, the muscle enzyme, was normal at 145, and your liver tests were normal.",
   "start": 124.04,
   "end": 160.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So what now? I really don't want those aches back.",
   "start": 160.82,
   "end": 163.5
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Totally understandable. muscle aches on statins are common and a lot of people do fine on a different statin at a lower dose. So I'd like to start Rosuvastatin 5 milligrams once a day and I'm adding Ezetimibe 10 milligrams once a day. It blocks cholesterol absorption in the gut and it doesn't cause muscle aches.",
   "start": 164.3,
   "end": 184.04
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Two new pills, huh?",
   "start": 184.48,
   "end": 185.62
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Yes, but together they should get you close to goal. If the aches come back stop the Rosuvastatin and send me a message but keep taking the ezetimibe.",
   "start": 186.54,
   "end": 195.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that I can do.",
   "start": 195.64,
   "end": 197.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "We'll recheck a lipid panel and liver tests in eight weeks. If your LDL is still above 55 after that, there are injectable cholesterol medicines we could talk about, but let's not get ahead of ourselves. Fair enough. Keep taking the aspirin and the clopidogrel through February, that's 12 months after the stent, and please don't stop the clopidogrel without talking to us first. Keep the metoprolol the same and keep up the walking.",
   "start": 198.29,
   "end": 224.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Well, do.",
   "start": 225.69,
   "end": 226.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So to sum up, you have coronary artery disease with a stent, which is stable and high LDL cholesterol, not at goal because you couldn't tolerate the atorvastatin. I'll see you back in three months. Thanks,",
   "start": 227.03,
   "end": 239.79
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Dr. Byan.",
   "start": 240.19,
   "end": 240.83
  }
 ],
